Give a town or city to another leader while you are at peace, or ask for one of theirs.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
Civilization VII lets settlements change hands in a deal only when a war ends. This mod opens the same deal screen in peacetime. Open a leader's diplomacy screen, click [b]Offer Settlement[/b], move settlements, gold or influence from either side into the deal, and propose it.

[list]
[*] An AI leader shows whether it would accept before you send the deal. The game makes that call, and the mod leaves the AI alone.
[*] A human player gets the deal screen and can accept, reject or change the deal, as with a peace deal.
[*] The deal goes through the game's own deal system, the same one peace deals use in multiplayer.
[/list]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
To play a game without the mod, tick No Settlement Gifting under Advanced Options, Game Options when you set it up.

Each player can also set these under Options, Mods, Settlement Gifting.
[list]
[*] Minimum Relationship: any, neutral, friendly, helpful, or allies only.
[*] Towns Only: keep cities out of deals.
[*] Include Capitals: list capitals as well. The game may still refuse them.
[*] Confirm Before Giving: ask before sending or accepting a deal that gives away your settlements.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*] The AI never offers you a settlement on its own.
[*] A settlement that changes hands gets the game's usual unrest for a transfer.
[*] In multiplayer every player needs the mod.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
The mod only changes the UI, so you can add it to a save or remove it at any time. It is built for game version 1.5.0. It wraps four named methods of the diplomacy screens instead of replacing game files, but a mod that replaces the peace deal screen may still conflict.

